d0e060b gated the line on "axis moving", but MotionDone() stays false while the 1203 is not up (safety circuit off -> EtherCAT slaves offline), so every pass still printed. Now W906IdxStop counts stops and prints one line per 30 s with how many stops happened and how many had the axis not reporting done; the stop itself is still sent every time as golden does. The earlier "still not fixed" was the F5 started 18:33 running old code.

Debug wb_serve 18:58 (new string present, old "was moving" gone), release 18:45. WORKLOG section 2 row 137 also records the safety PLC door bits mapped into D:\HT9045\system\IO_Table.csv (machine data, pushed in the machine_params snapshot; SafePlcIO stays 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Motor/myGALILmotor.cpp  | 22 +++++++++++-----------
 docs/WORKLOG_MACHINE.md |  1 +
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Motor/myGALILmotor.cpp b/Motor/myGALILmotor.cpp
index 76e4816..3af78a9 100644
--- a/Motor/myGALILmotor.cpp
+++ b/Motor/myGALILmotor.cpp
@@ -6578,18 +6578,18 @@ void W906IdxStop(TMyMotor& z, const char* why)
     //  (csystem.cpp, the G04 path) sends "ST" then "VS0;SP0,0,0,0;" to the Index EVERY pass (harmless on a Galil; the Galil route had a
     //  cooldown, AI(W906-INDEXZ-1203) D4).  The stop itself still runs every time (golden); the stdout line now says so only when the axis
     //  was moving, else one summary per 30 s with the count.
-    static unsigned long s_idle = 0, s_lastTick = 0;
+    //  EastSun 1006 (2nd screenshot, '-- was moving' on every line): MotionDone() is false while the 1203 card / axis is not up
+    //  (the safety circuit was open), so "moving" cannot gate the line.  Now: at most ONE line per 30 s, with the counts.
+    static unsigned long s_stops = 0, s_moving = 0, s_lastTick = 0;
     const unsigned long now = (unsigned long)::GetTickCount();
-    if (moving) {
-        std::printf("[IDX1203] %s stop (%s) -- was moving\n", z.Alias.c_str(), why ? why : "");
-    } else {
-        ++s_idle;
-        if (s_lastTick == 0 || now - s_lastTick >= 30000ul) {
-            std::printf("[IDX1203] %s stop (%s) on an idle axis -- %lu such stop(s) in the last %lu s (golden re-sends ST / VS0;SP0 every pass while the motor power is off)\n",
-                        z.Alias.c_str(), why ? why : "", s_idle, s_lastTick == 0 ? 0ul : (now - s_lastTick) / 1000ul);
-            s_idle = 0;
-            s_lastTick = now;
-        }
+    ++s_stops;
+    if (moving) ++s_moving;
+    if (s_lastTick == 0 || now - s_lastTick >= 30000ul) {
+        std::printf("[IDX1203] %s stop (%s) -- %lu stop(s) in the last %lu s, %lu with the axis not reporting done (golden re-sends ST / VS0;SP0 every pass while the motor power is off)\n",
+                    z.Alias.c_str(), why ? why : "", s_stops, s_lastTick == 0 ? 0ul : (now - s_lastTick) / 1000ul, s_moving);
+        s_stops = 0;
+        s_moving = 0;
+        s_lastTick = now;
     }
 }
 
